# Cut a release

Asking to cut a release is permission to commit the version bump, open the release PR and push the tag. Do not fold unrelated dirty files into that commit. `main` is protected: the bump reaches it only through a pull request.

1. Confirm `main` is clean and the intended work is already merged. Run `bun run test` if the bump commit includes more than version strings.
2. Read `workspace.package.version` in `Cargo.toml` and the latest `v*` tag (`git tag -l 'v*' --sort=-v:refname`). Use the version the user named, otherwise bump **patch**.
3. Branch `release/vX.Y.Z` from `main`. Set that **same** version in `Cargo.toml`, `apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`, `package.json`, and `apps/desktop/package.json`. Do not bump `rust-version` or crate names.
4. In `CHANGELOG.md`, turn `## [Unreleased] - Title` into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD - Title` (or add the section at the top), written for users. Run `bun run changelog:generate`. The release workflow reads this section as the release notes and fails the tag without it.
5. Commit only those files, with sign-off: `git commit -s -m "chore: release vX.Y.Z"`. Push the branch and open a pull request against `main`.
6. When the checks pass, merge the PR (ask first unless the user already said to merge). Then `git switch main && git pull`.
7. Annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` on the merged commit, then `git push origin vX.Y.Z`. The tag starts `.github/workflows/release.yml`. Pushing `main` without a tag does not ship.
8. Watch the release workflow. It has two jobs: macOS `publish` goes first, then `publish-windows` (signed NSIS installer). While the repository variable `WINDOWS_RELEASE_ENABLED` is not `true`, `publish-windows` shows as skipped; that is expected, not a failure. A failed job is fixed and re-run with **Re-run failed jobs**, never by retagging. Report the GitHub Release URL. Do not `tauri build` or sign locally.
9. If they asked to **try first**, keep the GitHub Release as a prerelease (`gh release edit vX.Y.Z --prerelease`). Promote with `--prerelease=false` when they want Latest. Installed apps follow non-prerelease Latest only.
10. **Never:** regenerate updater keys; change `com.bizzidb.app`; retag, delete or `--force` push a tag; skip the version bump or the changelog section; put secrets in the commit.
